NOTICE — Ft8Sharp

Credit
------

Ft8Sharp owes its structure and its constants to ft8_lib by Kārlis Goba
(https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib), an MIT-licensed C implementation of the FT8
and FT4 protocols. Without that work this library would not exist, and the debt
is acknowledged here rather than only in a commit message.

Citation
--------

The protocols themselves are described in:

    Franke K9AN, Somerville G4WJS, Taylor K1JT, "The FT4 and FT8 Communication
    Protocols," QEX, July/August 2020

Independent port
----------------

Ft8Sharp is an independent port. It is written in C# against the published
protocol description above and the structure of ft8_lib; it is not a derivative
distribution of ft8_lib, it is not affiliated with or endorsed by Kārlis Goba,
and it is not affiliated with or endorsed by the WSJT-X project or the authors
of the paper cited above. Errors in this library are its own.

Ft8Sharp is licensed under the MIT License; see the LICENSE file beside this
one. See porting-notes.md for the provenance of everything ported, including the
upstream commit this port is pinned to.
